cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CRASH3Vision in research, technical work, or academic publications, please cite this software using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "CRASH3Vision"
version: "1.0.1"
date-released: 2026-10-01

authors:
  - family-names: "Neves"
    given-names: "Bruno P."
    email: "bpn.bruno@gmail.com"

abstract: >-
  CRASH3Vision is experimental research software for semi-assisted measurement
  of vehicle structural deformation from calibrated digital images and
  estimation of deformation energy and Energy Equivalent Speed (EES) using
  CRASH3-derived methods. The software supports image calibration, reference
  and damaged-image alignment, W and C1-C6 deformation measurements, structural
  offset visualization, stiffness-coefficient management, deformation-energy
  calculation, EES estimation, project persistence, technical reporting, and
  traceable review of measurements. The current release accompanies a
  preliminary proof-of-concept evaluated with controlled NHTSA crash-test
  imagery and real-world UAV imagery.

